  "definitions": [
    {
      "id": "partition",
      "statement": "For N Majorana points counted with repetitions, the decreasing multiplicity list lambda=(m1,...,md), sum mi=N, is the degeneracy partition; d is the number of distinct points and maximal point multiplicity g=max mi.",
      "source": "mes-2014",
      "pdfPage": 4,
      "location": "SectionIII, afterEq24"
    },
    {
      "id": "slocc-invariant",
      "statement": "Invertible symmetric local filters act by a Mobius transformation on Majorana points and preserve their multiplicities. Thus a partition is constant within a symmetricSLOCCclass. It does not generally specify the class: d<=3 gives a singleclass, d>3 gives infinitelymanyclasses.",
      "source": "mes-2014",
      "pdfPage": 4,
      "location": "SectionIII; also symmetries-2015p7"
    },
    {
      "id": "ac-not-slocc-invariant",
      "statement": "Containing an AC representative does not make every state in aSLOCCclass AC. AC is preserved by collective rotations; eachSLOCCclass has at most one1-AC representative up to localunitaries.",
      "source": "symmetries-2015",
      "pdfPage": 7,
      "location": "SectionIV, openingparagraphs"
    },
    {
      "id": "pole-conditioning",
      "statement": "Rotate a point of multiplicityg to the southpole. In the source's increasing-m spinbasis, impose c_m=0 for m=-j,...,-j+g-1. These zeros impose multiplicity at leastg; one must check the next coefficient and all other roots before claiming the exactmaximal multiplicity.",
      "source": "measures-2017",
      "pdfPage": 9,
      "location": "SectionIVB, paragraphafterFigure6"
    },
    {
      "id": "convention",
      "statement": "Catalogue normalizedDicke convention is |D_N^r>=|j,j-r>, j=N/2. Source AppendixA lists increasing spinm, so its arrays must be reversed when copied into increasingDickeindexr. Multiplicity is unchanged by reflection/rotation, but coefficients should still carry an explicit convention.",
      "source": "measures-2017",
      "pdfPage": 11,
      "location": "Appendixopeningparagraph; alsoPRR2022p3Eq22"
    }
  ],
  "rigorousRestrictions": [
    {
      "id": "half-bound",
      "scope": "All pure symmetric states; and theirSLOCCclasses",
      "statement": "If any Majoranapoint has multiplicitym>=N/2, theSLOCCclass contains no1-ACstate, except for partition(N/2,N/2) whenN iseven. In thatexception theACrepresentative isbalancedDicke, up torotation.",
      "status": "publishedproof",
      "source": "mes-2014",
      "pdfPage": 4,
      "location": "SectionIII, Nonexistencecriterion anditsproof"
    },
    {
      "id": "higher-than-one",
      "scope": "Any t>=2",
      "statement": "ThebalancedDicke exception is1-AC butnot2-AC; therefore everyt>=2ACstate must have allmultiplicities strictlysmallerthanN/2.",
      "status": "publishedstatementwithdirectproof",
      "source": "symmetries-2015",
      "pdfPage": 7,
      "location": "SectionIVA"
    },
    {
      "id": "cyclic-existence",
      "scope": "SLOCCclasses containing a C_q-symmetric state, q>=2",
      "statement": "If everymultiplicity is<N/2 and theclass contains a C_q-symmetric state, it contains aunique(up toLU)1-ACrepresentative withthesameC_qsymmetry. It isconstructed bythepositive root ofsum_k(N-2k)|d_k|^2 y^k=0. This is anexistenceclaim about aclass, not anACclaim about everyclassmember and not a theorem about higherACorders.",
      "status": "publishedproof",
      "source": "symmetries-2015",
      "pdfPage": 7,
      "location": "SectionIVA,Eqs41-42"
    },
    {
      "id": "moment-reduction",
      "scope": "A t-ACstate witha pointofmultiplicityg",
      "statement": "Afterrotation to apole, Dickeprobabilities have truncatedsupport. DiagonalACconditions make theirfirstt moments equalto theuniformdistribution on0,...,N. This supplies rigorouslynecessary classicalmomentconstraints.",
      "status": "directdeductionfrompublishedcharacterization",
      "source": "symmetries-2015",
      "pdfPage": 4,
      "location": "Eqs16-17"
    },
    {
      "id": "two-ac-bound",
      "scope": "t>=2",
      "statement": "g<=(N-1)/3. In apoleframe with excitationX in[0,N-g], 2ACrequires EX=N/2 andvarX=N(N+2)/12. The elementaryvariancebound varX<=(EX)(N-g-EX) gives theclaim. Equality atN=3g+1 forces a two-pointdistribution and isattainedbyEq60.",
      "status": "independentcataloguededuction; notclaimedasaprooftheoreminPRA96",
      "source": "measures-2017",
      "pdfPage": 9,
      "location": "Eq60 suppliesattainment; momentcharacterizationfromsymmetries-2015p4"
    }
  ],
